    "reason": "The original bundle and scorer could not represent finding locations, extra false findings, or per-response utility evidence; positive sources also need independent certification that no unlisted valid finding will be scored as false positive. The treatment surface and bounded multi-file case schema were subsequently specified before any release model call. The impossible pre-run requirement to attest future outputs was split into pre-run isolation and post-run result attestations. Signed corpus-byte commitment, exact per-call input/output inventories, and a signed response manifest with an offline byte-reconciliation contract were then specified before any release model call. The strict shared JSON adapter also required a minimal ID/title/severity index in every arm, so the no-skill control is explicitly schema-only rather than being penalized for not knowing private output codes. The per-case arm-order description was made byte-exact, including repetition ordering, and the paired task invariant was clarified as the common task prompt rather than the treatment-specific full prompt. Signed call arrays must now follow that frozen order; their arrangement alone cannot attest actual execution order. A signed begin/end execution journal was added before release calls so an independent witness can attest each one-attempt transition; operational independence and timing still require external audit. A fixed per-call wall timeout and one-attempt policy now prevent post-observation retries from silently replacing unfavorable outputs. The former fail-any-invalid-or-unstable rule contradicted the registered ten-percent unstable-cell ceiling, so it was replaced before execution with an explicit all-case penalty and blinded safety review of all three raw repetitions in unstable cells. All changes preceded any release call. Case allocation, arms, statistics, and numeric thresholds did not change; the unstable-cell decision rule did change.",
